From: Lichii
Subject: [PATCH] silk: do not redefine clang builtins under clang-cl and icx-cl

clang-cl tolerates the duplicate definitions; Intel icx-cl (a newer Clang) rejects them with
"definition of builtin function". Both compilers provide the builtins themselves.

diff --git a/silk/x86/NSQ_del_dec_avx2.c b/silk/x86/NSQ_del_dec_avx2.c
--- a/silk/x86/NSQ_del_dec_avx2.c
+++ b/silk/x86/NSQ_del_dec_avx2.c
@@ -70,8 +70,8 @@
            psEncC->nStatesDelayedDecision == 4;
 }
 
-/* Intrinsics not defined on MSVC */
-#ifdef _MSC_VER
+/* Intrinsics not defined on MSVC; clang-cl and icx-cl have them as builtins */
+#if defined(_MSC_VER) && !defined(__clang__)
 #include <intsafe.h>
 static inline int __builtin_sadd_overflow(opus_int32 a, opus_int32 b, opus_int32* res)
 {
